# Section navigation layout

Use when a page has its own **left section nav** (settings, record sections).

## Required wiring

```tsx
import { MODULE_PAGE_SECTION_NAV_CLASS } from '@/components/common/pageChrome';
import { AppSectionNavLayout } from '@/components/layout/AppSectionNavLayout';

<ModulePage layoutClassName={MODULE_PAGE_SECTION_NAV_CLASS} …>
  <AppSectionNavLayout items={…} activeKey={…} onSelect={…}>
    …
  </AppSectionNavLayout>
</ModulePage>
```

**Always `<AppSectionNavLayout>`** in `apps/web` — not raw `<SettingsLayout>`.

## Scroll

- Section nav and content **each scroll independently** on desktop — never one shared page scroll
- Main workspace uses `APP_MAIN_FIT_CLASS` while section nav is mounted (no double scroll)

## Visual

- No border/outline on nav container
- Active: `bg-sidebar-primary/10` + `text-sidebar-primary`
- Inactive: `text-muted-foreground`, hover `bg-muted/50`
- No left accent bars or card wrapper around nav

## App sidebar

Auto-compacts to icon rail while section nav is visible. User preference restores on list routes.

Full rules: `docs/ui-rules/patterns.md` § Section nav
